IMPORT prelude

-- Marriage Act 1961 (Cth) -- who may marry: marriageable age and the under-18 order (ss 5 "minor", 11, 12), the consent of
-- parents to the marriage of a minor (s 13), the grounds on which a marriage is void (s 23B); who may solemnise: authorised
-- celebrants and where each may act (s 5 "authorised celebrant", ss 32, 39, 39F, 41); the notice of intended marriage and its
-- window of not earlier than 18 months and not later than 1 month before the marriage (s 42(1), (5)); the separate meeting
-- (s 42B), witnesses (s 44), the form of ceremony (s 45) and the explanation of marriage (s 46); which failures invalidate a
-- marriage and which do not (s 48); the certificates and the 14 days to forward the official one (s 50); legitimation by the
-- later marriage of a child's parents (s 89); and a religious ceremony between persons already married (s 113(1), (5)-(7),
-- with the offences in ss 99(6) and 101).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 34, compilation date 28 March 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 4, 2026), register id
-- C2026C00129, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1961A00012.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0013 in subjects/au/requirements.jsonl (priority 1), raised 6 times by the three Western
-- Australian cradle-to-grave scenarios: Chloe c025 (2021-03-14, turns 18: what can she do today that she could not
-- yesterday? -- s 11), c053 (2029-04-10, Notice of Intended Marriage lodged: how long before the wedding, how long is it good
-- for? -- ss 39, 42), c054 (2029-05-18, married in Kings Park by a civil celebrant with two witnesses: who may solemnise, who may
-- marry, what does the marriage register? -- ss 11, 13, 23B, 45, 50); Jake k055 (2033-08-10, Notice of Intended Marriage: how
-- long before? -- s 42), k056 (2033-09-16, married by a civil celebrant at the registry: who may solemnise, what does the
-- marriage do for a child born before it? -- ss 39, 45); Daniel d032 (2024-10-28, notice, a civil celebrant, and a Hindu
-- ceremony the week after: what makes the marriage valid, does the religious ceremony add anything? -- ss 42, 45, 48). SCOPED
-- to the provisions those events name, with the definitions, conditions and exceptions needed to answer them (s 5, ss 12, 32,
-- 39F, 41, 42B, 44, 46, 89, 113 and the offence sections they lead to).
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Persons whose consent is required (s 14 and Schedule 1), dispensation and consent by a magistrate or Judge
-- (ss 15-21) beyond their effect as inputs; the identification material, particulars and other matters PRESCRIBED by the
-- regulations for s 42 (INPUTS: the regulations are not deposited); the circumstances PRESCRIBED for shortening the notice
-- period under s 42(5) (an INPUT -- whether a prescribed authority has authorised it); the registers of ministers and celebrants,
-- celebrant registration, the registration charge, reviews and discipline (ss 26-39M); refusals by ministers, religious marriage
-- celebrants and religious bodies (ss 47-47B); foreign diplomatic and overseas marriages (Part IV Div 3, Part V, Part VA);
-- legitimation of children of foreign or void marriages and declarations (ss 90-92); offences other than ss 99(6) and 101;
-- void marriages before 1985 (s 23); the "prohibited relationship" (s 23B(2)-(6)) and "real consent" (s 23B(1)(d)) are INPUTS
-- (booleans), as are domicile and a party's belief.
--
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD as numbers. "1 month", "3 months" and "18 months" are counted as calendar months by moving the
-- month and keeping the day of the month; a day that does not exist in the target month (31 April) sorts after that month's
-- last day, so the earliest permitted day is the 1st of the next month. That convention is an INFERENCE; the Act does not say
-- how a month is counted and the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 is not deposited here. The 14 days in s 50(4) are counted as
-- calendar days after the day of solemnisation.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Marriage Act 1961 -- marriage`

§§ `dates`

GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year of` `d` MEANS FLOOR (`d` DIVIDED BY 10000)

GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month of` `d` MEANS FLOOR ((`d` MINUS (`the year of` `d` TIMES 10000)) DIVIDED BY 100)

GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day of the month of` `d` MEANS `d` MINUS (`the year of` `d` TIMES 10000) MINUS (`the month of` `d` TIMES 100)

-- The same day of the month, n calendar months later (n not negative).
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the date` `n` `months after` `d` MEANS
    ((`the year of` `d` PLUS FLOOR (`t` DIVIDED BY 12)) TIMES 10000) PLUS (((`t` MODULO 12) PLUS 1) TIMES 100) PLUS `the day of the month of` `d`
    WHERE
        `t` MEANS (`the month of` `d` MINUS 1) PLUS `n`

-- Days since 1 January 1970 of a YYYYMMDD date (the civil-from-days algorithm).
GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day number of` `d` MEANS
    (`era` TIMES 146097) PLUS `doe` MINUS 719468
    WHERE
        `y`   MEANS `the year of` `d`
        `m`   MEANS `the month of` `d`
        `yy`  MEANS IF `m` AT MOST 2 THEN `y` MINUS 1 ELSE `y`
        `era` MEANS FLOOR (`yy` DIVIDED BY 400)
        `yoe` MEANS `yy` MINUS (`era` TIMES 400)
        `mp`  MEANS IF `m` GREATER THAN 2 THEN `m` MINUS 3 ELSE `m` PLUS 9
        `doy` MEANS FLOOR (((153 TIMES `mp`) PLUS 2) DIVIDED BY 5) PLUS `the day of the month of` `d` MINUS 1
        `doe` MEANS (`yoe` TIMES 365) PLUS FLOOR (`yoe` DIVIDED BY 4) MINUS FLOOR (`yoe` DIVIDED BY 100) PLUS `doy`

-- Completed years of age on a day (a 29 February birthday is not modelled).
GIVEN `born on` IS A NUMBER, `on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age on the day` MEANS FLOOR ((`on` MINUS `born on`) DIVIDED BY 10000)

§§ `ss 5, 11, 12 -- marriageable age`

-- s 5(1): "minor means a person who has not attained the age of 18 years."
-- s 11: "Subject to section 12, a person is of marriageable age if the person has attained the age of 18 years."
-- s 12(1): a person who "has attained the age of 16 years but has not attained the age of 18 years may apply to a Judge or
-- magistrate ... for an order authorising him or her to marry a particular person of marriageable age"; (2) only if "the
-- circumstances of the case are so exceptional and unusual as to justify the making of the order"; (3) the applicant is then,
-- "in relation to his or her marriage to the other person specified in the order, but not otherwise, of marriageable age";
-- (5) the order "ceases to have effect" if the marriage "does not take place within 3 months after the date of the order".
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a minor` IF `age` LESS THAN 18

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may apply for a s 12 order` IF `age` AT LEAST 16 AND `age` LESS THAN 18

GIVEN `order made on` IS A NUMBER, `marriage on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 12 order is still in effect` IF `marriage on` AT MOST `the date` 3 `months after` `order made on`

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `has a s 12 order in effect for this marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is of marriageable age` IF
        `age` AT LEAST 18
    OR  `has a s 12 order in effect for this marriage`

§§ `s 13 -- consent to the marriage of a minor`

-- s 13(1): "where a party to an intended marriage, not having previously been married, is a minor, the marriage shall not be
-- solemnised unless there is produced to the person by whom the marriage is solemnised" the consent in writing of each person
-- whose consent is required, "duly witnessed and dated not earlier than 3 months before the date on which the marriage is
-- solemnised", or an effective consent of a magistrate or Judge, or a dispensation (who must consent: s 14 and Schedule 1,
-- not encoded). s 48(2)(f): failure to comply with s 13 does not invalidate the marriage; s 99(4) makes it an offence.
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `previously married` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `written consent must be produced under s 13` IF
    `the person is a minor` `age` AND (NOT `previously married`)

GIVEN `consent dated` IS A NUMBER, `marriage on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consent is dated recently enough` IF
    `the date` 3 `months after` `consent dated` AT LEAST `marriage on` AND `consent dated` AT MOST `marriage on`

§§ `ss 5, 32, 39, 39F, 41 -- who may solemnise, and where`

-- s 5(1): "authorised celebrant means ... in relation to a marriage proposed to be solemnised in Australia: (i) a minister of
-- religion registered under Subdivision A ...; (ii) a person authorised to solemnise marriages under Subdivision B ...; (iii)
-- a marriage celebrant; or (iv) a religious marriage celebrant".
-- s 32: a registered minister "may solemnise marriages at any place in Australia". s 39F: a registered marriage celebrant "may
-- solemnise marriages at any place in Australia" (a religious marriage celebrant is a registered marriage celebrant who is a
-- minister of religion: s 39DA). s 39(1): a person who under State law "has the function of registering marriages" may
-- solemnise marriages "in that State"; (2), (3) other State officers authorised by the Minister, "at any place in Australia or
-- only in the part or parts of Australia specified in the instrument".
-- s 41: "A marriage shall be solemnised by an authorised celebrant who is physically present at the place where the marriage
-- takes place and is authorised to solemnise marriages at that place."
-- s 29(a): only "a minister of religion of a recognised denomination" is registered under Subdivision A.
DECLARE Celebrant IS ONE OF
    `a minister of religion registered under Subdivision A`
    `a registered marriage celebrant`
    `a religious marriage celebrant`
    `a State registering officer under s 39(1)`
    `a State officer authorised under s 39(2)`
    `a person with no authorisation under the Act`

GIVEN `the celebrant` IS A Celebrant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an authorised celebrant` IF
    CONSIDER `the celebrant`
    WHEN `a person with no authorisation under the Act` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the celebrant` IS A Celebrant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a minister of religion` IF
    CONSIDER `the celebrant`
    WHEN `a minister of religion registered under Subdivision A` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a religious marriage celebrant` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the celebrant` IS A Celebrant, `the place is within the State or area of the authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the celebrant is authorised at the place` IF
    CONSIDER `the celebrant`
    WHEN `a minister of religion registered under Subdivision A` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a registered marriage celebrant` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a religious marriage celebrant` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a State registering officer under s 39(1)` THEN `the place is within the State or area of the authorisation`
    WHEN `a State officer authorised under s 39(2)` THEN `the place is within the State or area of the authorisation`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 46(1): an authorised celebrant "not being a minister of religion of a recognised denomination" must say the words
-- reminding the parties that marriage "is the union of 2 people to the exclusion of all others, voluntarily entered into for
-- life" (s 46(2): the Minister may exempt a s 39(2) officer). A religious marriage celebrant is not registered under
-- Subdivision A, so is treated here as not of a recognised denomination -- an INFERENCE (such a celebrant might belong to one).
GIVEN `the celebrant` IS A Celebrant, `exempted by the Minister under s 46(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the celebrant must explain the nature of marriage` IF
    CONSIDER `the celebrant`
    WHEN `a minister of religion registered under Subdivision A` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a State officer authorised under s 39(2)` THEN NOT `exempted by the Minister under s 46(2)`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 42 -- the notice of intended marriage`

-- s 42(1)(a): "a marriage shall not be solemnised unless ... notice in writing of the intended marriage has been given in
-- accordance with this section and has been received by the authorised celebrant solemnising the marriage not earlier than 18
-- months before the date of the marriage and not later than 1 month before the date of the marriage"; (b) evidence of each
-- party's date and place of birth; (c) each party's declaration "in the physical presence of that authorised celebrant" as to
-- conjugal status and "no legal impediment".
-- s 42(5): "Despite a notice ... having been received later than 1 month before the date of the marriage, a prescribed
-- authority may authorise an authorised celebrant to solemnise a marriage if the authority is satisfied that one or more of the
-- circumstances prescribed in the regulations have been met." (The circumstances are an INPUT.)
-- s 42(10): a divorced or widowed party must produce evidence of the divorce or death.
GIVEN `notice received on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earliest day the marriage may be solemnised` MEANS `the date` 1 `months after` `notice received on`

GIVEN `notice received on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day the notice supports a marriage` MEANS `the date` 18 `months after` `notice received on`

GIVEN `notice received on` IS A NUMBER, `marriage on` IS A NUMBER, `a prescribed authority authorised a shorter time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice was received in time` IF
        `marriage on` AT MOST `the last day the notice supports a marriage` `notice received on`
    AND (   `marriage on` AT LEAST `the earliest day the marriage may be solemnised` `notice received on`
         OR (`a prescribed authority authorised a shorter time` AND `notice received on` AT MOST `marriage on`))

§§ `ss 42B, 44, 45, 48 -- the ceremony, and what makes it valid`

-- s 42B: "An authorised celebrant must not solemnise a marriage unless the authorised celebrant has met separately with each
-- party before the intended marriage. The authorised celebrant and the party must be physically present at the meeting."
-- s 44: "at least 2 persons who are, or appear to the person solemnising the marriage to be, over the age of 18 years are
-- present as witnesses."
-- s 45(1): a minister of religion may use "any form and ceremony recognised as sufficient for the purpose by the religious body
-- or organisation"; (2) otherwise "it is sufficient if each of the parties says to the other, in the presence of the authorised
-- celebrant and the witnesses, the words: 'I call upon the persons here present to witness that I, A.B. (or C.D.), take thee,
-- C.D. (or A.B.), to be my lawful wedded wife (or husband, or spouse)'; or words to that effect."
-- s 48(1): "a marriage solemnised otherwise than in accordance with the preceding provisions of this Division is not a valid
-- marriage." (2): not invalid by reason of failures under s 42 (notice, declaration, birth evidence, "any other requirement of
-- section 42"), "the requirements of section 44 or 46", or "the requirements of section 13". (3): not invalid because the
-- person solemnising it was not authorised "if either party ... believed that that person was lawfully authorised", and then the
-- form is sufficient if it showed "an intention on the part of each of the parties to become thereby the lawfully wedded spouse
-- of the other".
-- s 42B is one of the "preceding provisions" and is NOT in the s 48(2) list. Read literally, a marriage solemnised without the
-- separate meetings is not valid. That is what is encoded; it is a reading of the words, not a decided point.
DECLARE Ceremony HAS
    `the celebrant` IS A Celebrant
    `the place is within the State or area of the authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the celebrant is physically present` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a party believed the person was lawfully authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the celebrant met each party separately and in person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the s 45 form or a recognised religious form was used` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the form showed each party's intention to become a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
    `witnesses over 18` IS A NUMBER
    `notice received on` IS A NUMBER
    `married on` IS A NUMBER
    `first party's age` IS A NUMBER
    `second party's age` IS A NUMBER
    `an under-age party has a s 12 order in effect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a party is lawfully married to someone else` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parties are within a prohibited relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a party's consent is not a real consent` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the ceremony` IS A Ceremony
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 41 is complied with` IF
        `the person is an authorised celebrant` (`the ceremony`'s `the celebrant`)
    AND `the ceremony`'s `the celebrant is physically present`
    AND `the celebrant is authorised at the place` (`the ceremony`'s `the celebrant`) (`the ceremony`'s `the place is within the State or area of the authorisation`)

GIVEN `the ceremony` IS A Ceremony
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there are enough witnesses under s 44` IF `the ceremony`'s `witnesses over 18` AT LEAST 2

GIVEN `the ceremony` IS A Ceremony
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the marriage is valid under s 48` IF
        (   (    `s 41 is complied with` `the ceremony`
             AND `the ceremony`'s `the s 45 form or a recognised religious form was used`)
         OR (    (NOT `the person is an authorised celebrant` (`the ceremony`'s `the celebrant`))
             AND `the ceremony`'s `the celebrant is physically present`
             AND `the ceremony`'s `a party believed the person was lawfully authorised`
             AND `the ceremony`'s `the form showed each party's intention to become a spouse`))
    AND `the ceremony`'s `the celebrant met each party separately and in person`

§§ `s 23B -- void marriages`

-- s 23B(1): a marriage "is void where: (a) either of the parties is, at the time of the marriage, lawfully married to some
-- other person; (b) the parties are within a prohibited relationship; (c) by reason of section 48 the marriage is not a valid
-- marriage; (d) the consent of either of the parties is not a real consent because" of duress or fraud, mistake as to identity
-- or the nature of the ceremony, or not understanding its nature and effect; "or (e) either of the parties is not of
-- marriageable age; and not otherwise."
GIVEN `the ceremony` IS A Ceremony
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the marriage is void under s 23B` IF
        `the ceremony`'s `a party is lawfully married to someone else`
    OR  `the ceremony`'s `the parties are within a prohibited relationship`
    OR  (NOT `the marriage is valid under s 48` `the ceremony`)
    OR  `the ceremony`'s `a party's consent is not a real consent`
    OR  (NOT `the person is of marriageable age` (`the ceremony`'s `first party's age`) (`the ceremony`'s `an under-age party has a s 12 order in effect`))
    OR  (NOT `the person is of marriageable age` (`the ceremony`'s `second party's age`) (`the ceremony`'s `an under-age party has a s 12 order in effect`))

-- s 99(1): an authorised celebrant "shall not solemnise a marriage ... in contravention of section 42 or 44" (6 months or 5
-- penalty units). The celebrant's offence and the marriage's validity come apart: a late notice or a missing witness is an
-- offence by the celebrant and leaves the marriage valid (s 48(2)).
GIVEN `the ceremony` IS A Ceremony, `a prescribed authority authorised a shorter time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the celebrant contravened s 42 or s 44 as to time and witnesses` IF
        (NOT `the notice was received in time` (`the ceremony`'s `notice received on`) (`the ceremony`'s `married on`) `a prescribed authority authorised a shorter time`)
    OR  (NOT `there are enough witnesses under s 44` `the ceremony`)

§§ `s 50 -- the certificates`

-- s 50(1): the celebrant prepares a certificate "for the purpose of issue to the parties" and "2 official certificates of the
-- marriage" ((1A): regulations may provide for only 1). (2): "Immediately after the solemnisation", the celebrant, each party
-- and "2 witnesses ... over the age of 18 years" sign each certificate. (4)(a)(i): "within 14 days after the solemnisation of
-- the marriage", forward one official certificate, with the notice, any s 12 order and the declarations, consents and
-- dispensations, "to the appropriate registering authority of a State or Territory ascertained in accordance with the
-- regulations". Registration itself is State law (for WA, the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998, not here).
-- s 45(3): the certificate is "conclusive evidence that the marriage was solemnised in accordance with" s 45, except where the
-- fact of the ceremony or a party's identity is in issue (s 45(4)).
GIVEN `married on` IS A NUMBER, `forwarded on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the official certificate was forwarded within 14 days` IF
        `the day number of` `forwarded on` MINUS `the day number of` `married on` AT MOST 14
    AND `forwarded on` AT LEAST `married on`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of people who sign each certificate` MEANS 5

§§ `s 89 -- legitimation by the later marriage of the parents`

-- s 89(1): "A child ... whose parents were not married to each other at the time of his or her birth but have subsequently
-- married each other ... is, by virtue of the marriage, for all purposes the legitimate child of his or her parents as from his
-- or her birth or the commencement of this Act, whichever was the later." (3): only if, at the time of the marriage (after the
-- 1985 amendment), "one of the child's parents was domiciled in Australia", or the marriage "took place in Australia" (or
-- under Part V or the Marriage (Overseas) Act 1955). (5): it does not affect property rights under a disposition or devolution
-- on a death before the marriage.
GIVEN `parents married to each other at the birth` IS A BOOLEAN, `parents later married each other` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a parent domiciled in Australia at the marriage` IS A BOOLEAN, `the marriage took place in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child is legitimated from birth by s 89` IF
        (NOT `parents married to each other at the birth`)
    AND `parents later married each other`
    AND (`a parent domiciled in Australia at the marriage` OR `the marriage took place in Australia`)

§§ `s 113 -- a religious ceremony between persons already married`

-- s 113(1): "Except in accordance with this section: (a) persons who are already legally married to each other shall not, in
-- Australia ... go through a form or ceremony of marriage with each other".
-- (5): "Nothing in this Act shall be taken to prevent 2 persons who are already legally married to each other from going through
-- a religious ceremony of marriage with each other in Australia where those persons have: (a) produced to the person by whom the
-- ceremony is to be performed a certificate of their existing marriage; and (b) furnished to that person a statement in writing,
-- signed by them and witnessed by that person" that they have married before, are the parties in the certificate, and have no
-- reason to believe they are not legally married.
-- (6): ss 42, 44, 50 and 51 "do not apply" to such a ceremony, and the person performing it shall not issue "any certificate of
-- marriage under or referring to this Act".
-- (7): a person who is not an authorised celebrant does not commit an offence against s 101 "by reason only of" performing a
-- religious ceremony between parties who have complied with (5).
-- s 99(6): a person authorised to solemnise marriages shall not, in contravention of s 113(1), purport to solemnise a marriage
-- between persons who inform the person, or whom the person knows or has reason to believe, to be already married to each other.
-- s 101: a person "shall not solemnise a marriage, or purport to solemnise a marriage, at a place in Australia ... unless the
-- person is authorised". Both: imprisonment for 6 months or 5 penalty units.
GIVEN `already legally married to each other` IS A BOOLEAN, `certificate of the existing marriage produced` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `signed and witnessed statement furnished` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the religious ceremony is within s 113(5)` IF
    `already legally married to each other` AND `certificate of the existing marriage produced` AND `signed and witnessed statement furnished`

GIVEN `officiant is an authorised celebrant` IS A BOOLEAN, `officiant knew or was told they were already married` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `certificate of the existing marriage produced` IS A BOOLEAN, `signed and witnessed statement furnished` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officiant of the second ceremony commits an offence` IF
        (NOT `the religious ceremony is within s 113(5)` TRUE `certificate of the existing marriage produced` `signed and witnessed statement furnished`)
    AND (    (NOT `officiant is an authorised celebrant`)
         OR  `officiant knew or was told they were already married`)
